HST Office: Word 97 (.doc) keeps macros written or edited in HST Writer (owner request, beta.5).

Saving as .doc copied only the VBA project read from the original file, so new macros were lost and
edits were dropped (with a generic warning). Like .docm and .xlsm, the document's current VBA-mode
Basic code is now written with oox::ole::VbaExport into the "Macros" storage of the .doc when the
project is new or was edited (BasicManager::IsBasicModified). An unchanged project, or an original
project with UserForms (which VbaExport cannot write), is still copied unchanged; for an edited one
with UserForms the existing "VBA code will not be saved" warning still appears.
- sw/source/uibase/app/docsh.cxx: also save the VBA storage for a VBA-mode document that did not
  come from a .doc (macros written in HST).
- sw/source/filter/ww8/wrtww8.cxx: SaveOrDelMSVBAStorage_ww8 writes the current project.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-vba.py (new document -> .doc: module kept and runs).
